*> Contract test, the core's consumer side of the C glue ABI (contracts/shim-abi.md §1, §5): every
*> CCSHIM.cpy constant the core uses (the outcomes, CC_ZLIB, CC_GZIP) has the contract's value, and
*> cc_deflate / cc_inflate link and behave per §5 (round trip, CC_SMALL, CC_BADDATA) with the
*> calling convention of research R2.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. CORE-CONTRACT-SHIM-CONSUMER.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CCSHIM.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-MODE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-INPUT               PIC X(3) VALUE "abc".
 01 WS-INPUT-LENGTH        BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-PACKED              PIC X(64).
 01 WS-PACKED-LENGTH       BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-UNPACKED            PIC X(64).
 01 WS-UNPACKED-LENGTH     BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-DEFLATE-RC          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-INFLATE-RC          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RC                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-GARBAGE             PIC X(8) VALUE "notzlib!".
 01 WS-GARBAGE-LENGTH      BINARY-LONG VALUE 8.
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "contract core shim consumer outcomes CC-AGAIN to CC-NOTFOUND are 1 to 7 (shim-abi §1, §3 to §7)"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 1234567 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = CC-AGAIN * 1000000 + CC-ADDR-IN-USE * 100000 + CC-UNRESOLVED * 10000
         + CC-CLOSED * 1000 + CC-SMALL * 100 + CC-BADDATA * 10 + CC-NOTFOUND
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "contract core shim consumer CC-ZLIB and CC-GZIP are 0 and 1 (shim-abi §5)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = CC-ZLIB * 10 + CC-GZIP
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-ZLIB TO WS-MODE
     MOVE "contract core shim consumer cc_deflate and cc_inflate mode CC_ZLIB return 0 and round trip"
         TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ROUND-TRIP
     MOVE CC-GZIP TO WS-MODE
     MOVE "contract core shim consumer cc_deflate and cc_inflate mode CC_GZIP return 0 and round trip"
         TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ROUND-TRIP

     MOVE "contract core shim consumer cc_deflate with a 1-byte capacity answers CC_SMALL" TO TL-CASE
     CALL STATIC "cc_deflate" USING BY VALUE WS-MODE BY REFERENCE WS-INPUT
         BY VALUE WS-INPUT-LENGTH BY REFERENCE WS-PACKED BY VALUE WS-ONE
         BY REFERENCE WS-PACKED-LENGTH RETURNING WS-RC
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE CC-SMALL TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-RC TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "contract core shim consumer cc_inflate of corrupt zlib data answers CC_BADDATA" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE CC-ZLIB TO WS-MODE
     CALL STATIC "cc_inflate" USING BY VALUE WS-MODE BY REFERENCE WS-GARBAGE
         BY VALUE WS-GARBAGE-LENGTH BY REFERENCE WS-UNPACKED BY VALUE WS-CAPACITY
         BY REFERENCE WS-UNPACKED-LENGTH RETURNING WS-RC
     MOVE CC-BADDATA TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-RC TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.

*> Expected "0 0 abc": both return codes 0 and the input back.
 ROUND-TRIP.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PACKED WS-UNPACKED
     MOVE 0 TO WS-UNPACKED-LENGTH
     CALL STATIC "cc_deflate" USING BY VALUE WS-MODE BY REFERENCE WS-INPUT
         BY VALUE WS-INPUT-LENGTH BY REFERENCE WS-PACKED BY VALUE WS-CAPACITY
         BY REFERENCE WS-PACKED-LENGTH RETURNING WS-DEFLATE-RC
     CALL STATIC "cc_inflate" USING BY VALUE WS-MODE BY REFERENCE WS-PACKED
         BY VALUE WS-PACKED-LENGTH BY REFERENCE WS-UNPACKED BY VALUE WS-CAPACITY
         BY REFERENCE WS-UNPACKED-LENGTH RETURNING WS-INFLATE-RC
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "0 0 abc" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-DEFLATE-RC TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-INFLATE-RC TO WS-EDIT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PACKED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " "
         WS-UNPACKED(1:FUNCTION MAX(WS-UNPACKED-LENGTH, 1)) DELIMITED BY SIZE
         INTO WS-PACKED
     MOVE WS-PACKED TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM CORE-CONTRACT-SHIM-CONSUMER.
